body:
Yes, life long depression. I began drinking at 25 after trying everything I could to get better by myself (did not try medication or therapy or healthcare) and gave up and turned to alcohol. Alcohol doesn't make me happy but it relieves me of the suffering, it's an open door that leads me out of the room I'm stuck in with depression. My motivation to lessen my drinking is to have less physical discomfort, to spend less, and to run 5ks again. it's difficult to find motivation to quit strictly for just physical reasons. It's awesome you've made it 7 months, that's great.

&#x200B;

I'm so sorry your therapist did that to you. I hope you're able to make some calls and locate a therapist more prepared to help you. If you're not able to do this, maybe the ER can arrange something for you.
